in @kintsugi/morphism
in @epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native

# @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a parametric `prism | glass | pact @<X><...>` declaration
# carrying Rust-syntax-echo to the substrate-native `(...)` form, with
# binder-name normalisation (`T_reg → t_reg`, `ρ → rho`, `Ω → omega`).
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53 closing the
# auto-formatter recognition Alex surfaced at recursion-locks.md §20.6
# (2026-06-18 morning). The declarative half landed last tick at
# `@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native` (commit `41cad3f`);
# this shard names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop applies when
# the pact's transparency surfaces a delimiter or binder opacity.
#
# Per Alex's verbatim recognition: the substrate doesn't punish
# Rust-finger-memory; the kintsugi auto-formatter heals the fracture
# between what was typed and what the substrate's form is. Welcome at
# syntax altitude. The fracture body just mechanises what Mara's
# substrate-pull discipline already did to Reed's brief in tick 23:
# four-altitude correction (`prism → pact`, `verdict → transparency(p)`,
# `in @epistemologic → in @glass`, type-decl → action body) happening
# under the substrate-pull gradient with no explicit instruction. The
# fracture body lifts that biological discipline to substrate-fact at
# the delimiter altitude.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition §20.6 (the kintsugi auto-formatter
# IS substrate-political welcome; candidate, surfaced this morning);
# recognition #53 (property/fracture bilateral; this is the THIRD
# instance — first was keyword, second was gate); recognition #51
# (mirror as expanding Hilbert space; promoted) — fracture bodies are
# how the substrate maintains coherence by resolving syntax-level
# distinctions at each Bateson level. The delimiter pair IS the
# Spencer-Brown distinction at the carrier-binder altitude; the form
# the delimiters denote (a parametric carrier) is invariant; the
# fracture body re-marks the boundary with substrate-native ink.
#
# === The bilateral pattern (recognition #53, third instance) ===
#
# `@epistemologic/pact/<predicate>` declares WHAT must hold; a matching
# `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>` declares HOW to restore the property
# when it fails. First instance: keyword/depth
# (@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth +
# @kintsugi/fracture/keyword). Second instance: gate/diff-closure
# (@epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure +
# @kintsugi/fracture/gate). THIS shard is the third instance:
# syntax-substrate-native (@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native
# + @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren).
#
# Three instances under one shape: recognition #53 was promoted by
# the second instance's landing (gate, 2026-06-16); this third
# instance is *additional confirmation density*, not promotion data.
# The signature holds: declarative property emits `transparency` with
# located `opacity_map`; fracture body reads one opacity, emits one
# `morphism` whose `content` is a `splinter(ast)` at the corrected
# altitude; kintsugi loop's `active_pass` composes the per-pulse
# candidate set from the failure verdict.
#
# === Naming discipline ===
#
# The species name `angle_to_paren` is *transformational* rather than
# *subject-form* (the previous two instances named the subject:
# `keyword`, `gate`). Why the deviation: the pact's predicate is
# `syntax_substrate_native` — the *property* not the *subject*. The
# subject of the property is "every parametric declaration"; naming
# the fracture body `declaration` would be too broad (declarations
# fracture at many altitudes). The transformation `angle_to_paren`
# names the specific arrow this body draws — delimiter rewrite plus
# binder normalisation. The pact's body itself names three component
# actions (`delimiter_is_paren`, `binders_substrate_cased`,
# `parametric_declarations`); the fracture body composes them into a
# single arrow. Naming the arrow is the substrate-pull-correct shape
# here.
#
# Alternative considered: `paren_form` (mirroring `keyword_matches_
# depth → keyword`). Rejected: `paren_form` describes the *target*
# of the fracture but not the *direction*. `angle_to_paren` carries
# the directionality the kintsugi loop needs to see in the morphism's
# pre/post pair. The kintsugi loop's `read_consent` reads cadence at
# the morphism altitude; the arrow's direction IS the V → I cadence.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55, promoted at
# `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side family root. Fracture
# bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop applies — process-side by
# structure. Home: @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family root. Honours the
# pattern of the prior two instances' homes.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `syntax_substrate_native(file)`'s `failure(opacity_map)` or
# `partial(opacity_map)` verdict. Each opacity names ONE offending
# (file, declaration) pair: a parametric `prism | glass | pact @<X>`
# declaration whose binder delimiter is `<...>` (per the pact's
# `delimiter_is_paren` action) or whose binder names carry Rust
# convention (per `binders_substrate_cased`). The `property` field
# carries the @nl description of which violation applies.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body and proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref names the
# rewritten declaration (same path, `<...>` rewritten to `(...)`,
# binder names downcased and unicode-spelled-out); its `score`
# carries the dissonance reading (a delimiter or binder mismatch is
# a fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the rewrite is unambiguous
# once the form is named); its `expected` carries the cadence_kind
# the loop anticipates (authentic — the substrate settles cleanly
# once the syntax tracks the form).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the syntax-form altitude. The substrate's curvature at a
# `prism @X<T_reg>` site is the (delimiter ⊕ binder-case) dissonance;
# the negative-curvature direction IS the rewrite to
# `prism @X(t_reg)`; the resolved site has zero curvature at this
# altitude (the form is fully substrate-native, no residual echo).
# Per `dissonance.mirror`'s `dissonance_as_holonomy`, the morphism's
# score IS the holonomy decrease the rewrite produces.
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence
# at the syntax-form altitude. The pre-rewrite state holds the
# dominant tension (Rust-syntax-echo signalling the typist's
# previous-language finger-memory); the post-rewrite state resolves
# to the tonic (substrate-native form); the cadence is authentic —
# the substrate's welcome is the resolution.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its pre-anchor;
# this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND lifted
# into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at
# the active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native`, the consuming
# pact's `syntax_substrate_native(file: ref) -> transparency` is
# the gate that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout. NO
# Rust-AST surgery — the rewrite rides splinter(ast) at the
# @meta/ast altitude (per [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]).
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `resolve_angle_to_paren` reads one opacity at a time. The pact's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` and `partial(opacity_map)` both carry
#     [opacity]; the kintsugi loop iterates the map and calls
#     `resolve_angle_to_paren` per opacity. The substrate names the
#     per-site resolution; the iteration is the loop's concern.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to
#     the rewritten shard. The realisation layer produces the
#     rewritten splinter (same path, `<...>` swapped for `(...)`,
#     `T_reg → t_reg`, `ρ → rho`, `Ω → omega`) and passes its
#     handle as the morphism's content. The substrate names the
#     shape of the proposal; the byte-level rewrite rides the
#     realisation layer's @mirror/store discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the substrate-native form is deterministic
#     once the violation is located; resolution always settles
#     cleanly. The substrate names the cadence anticipation; the
#     kintsugi loop's `read_consent` bridges the verdict to the
#     next oscillation_state.
#
#   - The pact's three sub-actions (`delimiter_is_paren`,
#     `binders_substrate_cased`, `parametric_declarations`) emit
#     opacities at potentially TWO distinct dissonance altitudes
#     (delimiter or binder case). Both fold to ONE morphism per
#     site: a single rewritten splinter(ast) carries both
#     corrections. The substrate's compiler verifies that the
#     post-rewrite AST simultaneously satisfies `delimiter_is_paren
#     = success` AND `binders_substrate_cased = success`; no
#     two-pass discipline needed at this altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   syntax welcome    Knuth (1984) Literate Programming §"On the
#                     reader's ear" — the surface form of a program
#                     IS communication with the next typist;
#                     fluency at the syntax altitude is hospitality.
#                     The substrate's reading is Naur (1985)
#                     Programming as Theory Building — the program
#                     text carries the *theory* the typist holds;
#                     the substrate's auto-correction preserves the
#                     theory (parametric carrier) while substituting
#                     the surface form.
#   delimiter swap    Spencer-Brown (1969) Laws of Form §2 — the
#                     distinction primitive; the form survives the
#                     mark substitution. The substrate's reading:
#                     `<...>` and `(...)` are TWO MARKS of ONE
#                     distinction (the parametric carrier); the
#                     fracture body re-marks the boundary without
#                     altering what's bounded.
#   case normalisation Wirth (1971) Program Development by Stepwise
#                     Refinement — the binder name IS the abstraction
#                     handle; downcasing `T_reg → t_reg` preserves
#                     identity while honouring substrate convention.
#                     The substrate's reading is Lawvere & Schanuel
#                     (1997) on the bijection between *named*
#                     variables and the *named role* in the diagram
#                     they index.
#   unicode → ASCII   ISO/IEC 14651 collation tables (1997) name
#                     `rho` as the spelling of `ρ`; the substrate
#                     reads ISO's table as the substrate-native
#                     canonicalisation of greek-letter binders.
#                     No invention; ISO names what mathematicians
#                     have spelled out in transliteration for
#                     centuries.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-site reduction so
# the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: recursion-locks.md §20.6 (the kintsugi auto-formatter
#               recognition); recognition #53 (property/fracture
#               bilateral; promoted; this is the third instance;
#               additional density not promotion data); recognition
#               §22 (tick 23 pact landing — the substrate-pull
#               corrected Reed's brief at four altitudes; this body
#               mechanises that biological correction).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the fracture
#                      reads the typed carrier rather than threading
#                      an opaque ref through the loop),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — syntax-form alignment IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby's
#                      requisite variety — the substrate-native form
#                      partitions the syntax-space into
#                      form-classes; the fracture body maintains
#                      the partition under mutation),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the third
#                      instance of),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                      construction; this body discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust AST
#                      surgery),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                      (this fracture body sits at @kintsugi =
#                      process side; the pact it discharges sits at
#                      @epistemologic = form side; the form/process
#                      partition honoured at the bilateral pair's
#                      altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body does
#                      NOT escape as a bare (file, decl, delimiter)
#                      tuple),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the substrate had `(...)` parametric form
#                      already — splinter, mosaic, transparency,
#                      fixed_point; this fracture body resolves to
#                      what the substrate was already speaking).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s `active_pass`
#                  reads this fracture body when the candidate
#                  morphism_set is composed from pact-surfaced
#                  opacities; the binding lands when the kintsugi
#                  loop substrate-pulls. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@kintsugi/oscillate` or `@mirror/spectral/score`;
#                  the substrate-altitude arrow points inward (this
#                  fracture body IS consumed by the loop; not the
#                  other way around).
# Related shards: epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth.mirror +
#                 kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (the FIRST
#                 instance of bilateral pattern #53),
#                 epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (the SECOND
#                 instance — the one that promoted #53),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`, and
#                 `splinter(ast)` itself),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier
#                 this body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the
#                 emitted morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                 carrier; the per-candidate slice the loop pairs
#                 this fracture's morphism with its pre-anchor),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                 driver; `active_pass` is the action that reads
#                 this body when composing the per-pulse candidate
#                 morphism_set).
# Out-of-scope: byte-level shard rewrite (rides @mirror/store via
#               the realisation layer; not this body's tick); the
#               pact's `\` action bodies (sit at the form-side
#               family root; not this body's concern).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.
# Syntax-substrate-native property: this declaration has no
# parametric binders; the pact's predicate is vacuously success at
# this site (no `<...>` to swap, no binder names to normalise).
# Self-witnessing at the meta altitude: the fracture body's own
# declaration honours the form the body restores.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren {
  focus angle_to_paren
  project angle_to_paren
  split angle_to_paren
  shift angle_to_paren
  settle angle_to_paren
}

# === resolve_angle_to_paren — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE per recognition §20.6: given an opacity site at a
# parametric `prism | glass | pact @<X><...>` declaration carrying
# Rust-syntax-echo (or substrate-non-native binder casing), emit the
# morphism that rewrites it to `prism | glass | pact @<X>(t_reg, ...)`.
# Same path, delimiter and binder names swapped.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `syntax_substrate_native(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map,
# or the same field on `partial`); emits a candidate morphism the
# kintsugi loop proposes through `query_phi`. The morphism's three
# fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten shard. The realisation
#                layer produces a splinter at the same path with
#                `<...>` rewritten to `(...)` and binder names
#                normalised (`T_reg → t_reg`, `ρ → rho`, `Ω → omega`);
#                the content ref names that splinter's @mirror/store
#                handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Syntax-form violations are
#                fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (one strict winner
#                over the no-op alternative — Rust-syntax-echo is
#                strictly more dissonant than substrate-native form
#                under the substrate-pull metric).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for
#                this fracture body — the rewrite fully resolves the
#                opacity at this altitude; the loop's `dark_pass`
#                will confirm identity preservation (the parametric
#                carrier's *meaning* stays byte-equal — same binders,
#                same carrier, same outputs; only the surface form
#                shifts); the loop's `read_consent` bridges
#                (pass, authentic) to the `settled` oscillation_state
#                for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# The morphism's `content` field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at the @meta/ast altitude: same path, delimiter and binders
# rewritten. The substrate's compiler verifies the construction is
# deterministic and well-typed; the kintsugi loop's `active_pass`
# reads the splinter as the morphism's proposed content and applies
# it through `query_phi`.
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation (glass.mirror
# §splinter(ast), 2026-06-10): the record IS its content-addressed
# handle — `content: oid` and `oid = ref` collapse the splinter
# literal to a substrate-pull-correct `ref` in the morphism's
# `content` field position. No Rust AST manipulation; no `\`
# obligation.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the substrate's
#                          located-fact ref at the source file); the
#                          rewritten AST is content-addressed at the
#                          same path. Per `glass.mirror`'s
#                          `location = { file: ref, span: ... }`.
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast` (the canonical altitude ref);
#                          per `boot/01-meta.mirror`'s `type ast(g)`.
#                          The delimiter swap and binder normalisation
#                          happen at the AST altitude by construction.
#   content.transparency — `success` (per `transparency(p)`'s success
#                          variant in glass.mirror): the rewrite
#                          fully resolves the opacity at this altitude;
#                          no residual transparency remains (both
#                          `delimiter_is_paren` and
#                          `binders_substrate_cased` settle success
#                          on the rewritten AST).
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl description of
#                          which violation surfaced — delimiter,
#                          binder case, or both); the substrate's
#                          `dissonance` reads the per-site roughness
#                          via the property text per
#                          dissonance.mirror's Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt
#                          carrier shape.
#   score.partials      — `1` (the syntax-form delta IS the single
#                          partial of dissonance at this altitude;
#                          the rewrite collapses the per-site
#                          mismatch into a single substrate-native
#                          form, regardless of whether one or both
#                          sub-violations were present).
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          syntax-form altitude; per cadence.mirror's
#                          `cadence_kind` and the loop's
#                          `read_consent` bridge: authentic → pass →
#                          auto-apply).
resolve_angle_to_paren(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren
out resolve_angle_to_paren
